<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00008260> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00008260> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1522-9900" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-30"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "GPR179 and RGS9BP organize RGS7/RGS11-Gbeta5 GAP activity on Galpha-o to enable TRPM1 gating in ON-bipolar cells_Visual Perception (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ,
                                                                                   "https://www.uniprot.org" ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Curated with GO AI HUB. GPR179 and RGS9BP anchor the RGS7/RGS11-Gbeta5 GAPs that deactivate Galpha-o, enabling TRPM1 opening in ON-bipolar cells."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "PROTOTYPE (curator design, 2026-10-19). GAP activities enabled_by RGS7 / RGS11 (catalytic subunit known: GO-CAM complex guideline case 1); GNB5 isoform 2 (Gbeta5S) as its own molecular function activator activity (GO:0140677) upstream of each GAP; RGS9BP as protein-membrane adaptor activity (GO:0043495), as in production 6a18a9ba00000549 / 6a2b236300000742. RGS7 / RGS11 GAP units (2026-10-23): ISS GO_REF:0000024 with mouse Rgs7 MGI:1346089 / Rgs11 MGI:1354739; basis Cao 2009 PMID:19625520 (Fig. 8 GAP on Galpha-o; Figs. 1B, 3A tips) and Cao 2012 PMID:22547806 (Figs. 3-4 double KO, IGI; Figs. 1C, 2B tips), per-fact detail in each evidence comment."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

